  "body": "**[Original report](https://bitbucket.org/agriggio/art/issues/181) by Paul Matthijsse (Bitbucket: [Paul Matthijsse](https://bitbucket.org/Paul Matthijsse), ).**\n\n----------------------------------------\n\nHello, some little things about the Resize option.\n\n1. Why does the Applies to: option default to Cropped Area when I haven’t made a crop at all? The default should be Applies to Full Image imo.  \n2. When I choose Scale and set the slider to 2.0 and save the file, the pixel dimensions are still the same. I have to tick Allow upscaling to make this work. What is the use of this? I already said ‘upscale 2x’, so upscale 2 times!\n3. When using that scale slider, the values in the PPI= field aren’t updated automatically, I have to change the ppi value \\(eg. from 300 to 299\\) to see the actual output values. \n\n‌\n",
